  "description": "Sadman Ahmed Shanto is a USC Physics PhD candidate, experimental physicist, and research engineer whose work spans quantum processor R&D, superconducting-device design and fabrication, cryogenic measurement, quasiparticle physics, scientific machine learning, autonomous experimentation, and research software. His experience includes the Levenson-Falk Lab, Google Quantum AI, Quantum Elements Inc., particle-detector instrumentation, and computational transportation research. He is also the creator and lead developer of SQuADDS.",
